# Tonal — Changelog

## v1.0.4 — Spectrum Analyzer

- Added real-time spectrum analyzer to the Equalizer page (GStreamer-based)
- 512-point FFT mapped to 31-band 1/3 octave display (ISO center frequencies)
- Peak hold markers with configurable hold time and decay
- Smooth bar animation with instant rise and gradual falloff
- Automatic start/stop lifecycle tied to application window
- Graceful degradation when GStreamer is unavailable
- Dark/light theme support matching existing VU meter style

## v1.0.3 — Version Display

- Added application version display to the Status page
- Version sourced from constants.py for single-source-of-truth consistency

## v1.0.2 — Phase 1 Refactor

- Centralized shared constants into constants.py (channel targets, file paths, filter types, sample rate)
- Extracted duplicated helpers into widgets/helpers.py (scrollable_wrap, block_scroll, load_themed_svg_icon, icon_button)
- Moved inline CSS from tonal.py to data/style.css
- Replaced magic strings with named constants across all modules
- Updated build script to include new files

## v1.0.1 — Bug Fixes

- Bug fixes and minor improvements

## v1.0.0 — Initial Release

- Multi-channel PipeWire routing for RODECaster Pro II (Expanded/Standard/USB 2)
- Parametric EQ with unlimited bands and 8 filter types
- Profile management (save, switch, delete, auto-backup)
- Import from EasyEffects JSON and Peace profiles
- Export to EqualizerAPO and EasyEffects formats
- Per-application audio routing rules with app discovery
- Real-time VU meter with peak hold and EQ peak overlay
- Live EQ updates without PipeWire restart
- Hardware auto-detection (USB 1 Expanded/Standard, USB 2)
- Zero Python package dependencies
- .deb package with desktop integration
